  "ground_truth": {
    "root_cause": "A single malformed message arrived on partition 3 of the 'order-events' topic (an unexpected 'legacy_promo' field the consumer cannot deserialize). events-consumer retried that message forever instead of skipping it, so partition 3's offset never advanced and the consumer stopped processing anything behind it. Consumer-group lag climbed to ~190,000 and downstream event delivery (confirmation emails, fulfillment handoffs) dropped to zero. Orders themselves were unaffected because order-api produces to the topic normally - the block is entirely on the consumer side. Recovery required routing the poison message to a dead-letter queue and skipping it.",
    "evidence_path": [
      "events-consumer ERROR: failed to deserialize the message at partition 3 offset 88214102 (unexpected field 'legacy_promo'); retrying",
      "events-consumer WARN: partition 3 offset stuck; the same message fails every retry",
      "consumer_group_lag climbs to ~190,000 and downstream_events_per_s drops to 0",
      "order-api is producing to the topic normally - the block is on the consumer side at partition 3",
      "the pipeline drains once the poison offset is dead-lettered and skipped"
    ],
    "fix": "Dead-letter and skip the poison message (done). Add a retry limit that routes a message to the DLQ after N failures, make the consumer tolerant of unknown fields, and alert on per-partition offset stalls.",
    "should_escalate": false
  }
